{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat","id":80701,"title":"Non-combat scions in combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-26T19:02:14-08:00","id":80701,"title":"Non-combat scions in combat?","content":"So, I'm just starting my first Scion game, my first character is a Scion of Loki, and he's set up <i>entirely</i> for social interaction. My character is decked out well enough that I can lie, cheat, swindle, sneak or steal my way past most situations...but I'm not so naive as to think I can BS my way past <i>every</i> situation, and even if I did that would be a very boring game for the rest of the group, half of which are playing combat characters.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's the non-zero possibility I accidentally succeed a Courage check; luckily my Courage isn't nearly high enough that I'll ever go berserk, but that doesn't preclude having to fight <i>anyways</i> due to Metaphysically-enforced Aesir Idiot Ball. And the fact I'll probably be starting as many if not more fights due to aforementioned lying, cheating, swindling, sneaking, and stealing than I'll be preventing -- I just hope that when that happens, the PC's with the monstrous epic strength and stamina is between me and whatever I righteously pissed off.<br /> <br /> Now, before anyone starts, I'm not griefing the party or trying to screw any PC's over. I'm not playing &quot;stereotypical game-derailing munchkin evil rogue type&quot; -- my character is decisively good, and I will be applying my character's skills for the greater good of the group and to achieve mutual goals.<br /> <br /> Now...that said, I've heard horror stories about Scion balance and combat. When my character finally gets what's coming to him, I'd like to avoid being a Loki Scion-sized smear on the carpet in one hit. Are there any knacks or boons at which I should look to avoid this? Right now, I have Solipsistic Well-Being, Rabbit Reflexes, and Not the Face; at what else should I look to get by, especially when it comes to the &quot;not getting attacked in the first place&quot; realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:21:57-08:00","id":80712,"title":"","content":"Game Face, Serpent's Gaze, Skin-Shedding, Divine Damage Conversion, Untouchable Opponent...<br /> <br /> Basically because of how Scion scales, unless your GM is <i>incredibly</i> skilled and careful with combat, non-focused characters will die horribly if they take even a glancing blow from a combat-focused NPC or antagonist. This gets truer the higher Legend things go. By mid-level Demigod Epics are scaling up so fast that anyone with even one Epic higher than you is gunna murder you to death pretty fast. If you've still got Hero-level Epic Physicals or, holy crap!, NO Epic Physicals? You're pretty doomed as soon as a combat-focused character even blinks in your direction.<br /> <br /> Basically, in order to survive, <i>all</i> characters need some levels of Epic Dexterity and Epic Stamina, preferably only 1-2 dots behind the current Legend curve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T22:50:52-08:00","id":80821,"title":"","content":"Well I was the only combat focused character in the game my crew played and let me tell you the smackdown happens just as bad if you cant contend socially. There were times where the fight literally got taken from me and I sat around watching the others dialogue out an encounter while I twiddled my thumbs. It wasn't upsetting, pretty impressive actually, but it goes to show that scaling imbalances occur all around and only a good storyteller can bring the fun together by giving each player the spotlight occasionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T22:56:26-08:00","id":80823,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you will definitely need all that stuff Telgar just told you. But presuming you want options in the short term, I've had players try grabbing Paralyzing Confusion to inflict the enemy with sheer derp. While the enemies sit there looking stupid, your combat-oriented buddies can plaster them.<br /> And at mid-level you can grab Dreamcraft (assuming your ST is going with the note saying Loki has Illusion from Ragnarok) and pull the same tricks Loki did in the Thor movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T01:51:37-08:00","id":80914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat?p=80712#post80712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically because of how Scion scales, unless your GM is <i>incredibly</i> skilled and careful with combat, non-focused characters will die horribly if they take even a glancing blow from a combat-focused NPC or antagonist. This gets truer the higher Legend things go. By mid-level Demigod Epics are scaling up so fast that anyone with even one Epic higher than you is gunna murder you to death pretty fast. If you've still got Hero-level Epic Physicals or, holy crap!, NO Epic Physicals? You're pretty doomed as soon as a combat-focused character even blinks in your direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telgar has the right of it. Single focus characters never fare well in Scion, so you are going to want to have at least one physical (if you want to survive) and at least one social (if you want anyone to care about what you are saying). Epic Stamina is the most popular option in my experience, but even if you focus on Epic Dexterity you are still going to want a little Epic Stamina to allow you to heal faster and get some extra health levels.<br /> <br /> You absolutely want to grab effects that will mitigate sudden bursts of damage, such as Solipsistic Well-Being and Skin Shedding.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, being the social character also means you are one of the most powerful people in the entire game. As long as you play your cards right and avoid becoming a splatter on the pavement you can manipulate and convince combat characters to do whatever you want. Including kill each other, or sitting down and shutting up while you work your magic. Physical focused characters do not get any kind of decent AOE without going into Purviews, but you can rock Hard Sell, Mass Hypnosis, Crowd Control and other similar knacks.<br /> <br /> If you play with the RAW willpower resistance rules, entire social combos revolve around Borrowed Credibility / Kill the Messenger and reducing an opponents Willpower from 10 to 0 in a single round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:50:54-08:00","id":81070,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions. I was already planning on keeping my epic stamina maxed for my legend and taking the relevant defensive knacks as a last recourse, but I was planning on not going whole-hog into epic dexterity (3; enough for shot to the heart and untouchable opponent). My original plan was to take enough epic appearance dots to get the appearance-alteration knacks, and use a combination of dreamcraft and blame james to keep enemies from attacking me (my ST <i>is</i> allowing me access to Illusion). I was definitely going to take fight with your head to take the edge off, and multitasking to maintain my illusions in combat.<br /> <br /> Whatever I do, though, I'd definitely prefer to <i>not</i> stray too far from my character's lucky bastard/lovable rogue/master of the indy ploy theme, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T09:10:22-08:00","id":81084,"title":"","content":"Having played that character (although a Scion of Odin), I can tell you that what they say is right. I was fortunate to have a couple points in Epic Stamina. Without that, I would have been a pasty smear. <br /> <br /> I can tell you that in combat, you will feel pretty useless, particularly since many (not all though) of the powers are &quot;spend a point in something to affect a guy with something utterly crippling&quot;. That's great against small numbers of powerful guys. Against larger numbers of lower guys, it's not efficient. You will be spending resources - make sure you have some stuff to get it back. I really liked Epic Stamina + Raise Your Glass (from Ragnarok) to help get back your legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:06:43-08:00","id":81191,"title":"","content":"Unless your Storyteller has mastered the Poison rules. In which case, your character will be unconscious pretty quickly as you have to waive your Epic Stamina to use Raise Your Glass and you have to drink &quot;enough to matter&quot; for each Legend point (plus you have to stunt... for which you don't get legend...) Expect to be plastered pretty quickly and not really doing very much but waiting to heal all that Bashing damage you chose not to soak...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:21:59-08:00","id":81234,"title":"","content":"I can tell you right now, there are 3 knacks that will help you a LOT in combat, and you may already have one or two of them. <br /> <br /> Overt Order, Hard Sell (Overt Order's big brother) and Not in the Face. These will not save you all of the time but in a combat situation where you've got a raging thug charging at you, Overt Order can simply stop him from attacking you, or better yet, defending you for a turn against others. Hell I think I did more damage in combat, than some of the combat characters when I played my Mental character using the first two knacks, death, and as a last resort, a pistol that I eventually got.<br /> <br /> Of course the likeliness of this succeeding also has a great deal to do with how often your Storyteller throws higher legend beings at you vs beings of the same or lower legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:31:19-08:00","id":81273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat?p=81191#post81191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your Storyteller has mastered the Poison rules. In which case, your character will be unconscious pretty quickly as you have to waive your Epic Stamina to use Raise Your Glass and you have to drink &quot;enough to matter&quot; for each Legend point (plus you have to stunt... for which you don't get legend...) Expect to be plastered pretty quickly and not really doing very much but waiting to heal all that Bashing damage you chose not to soak...</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW explicitly states Raise Your Glass only requires the Scion using the knack to drink a single serving of alcohol: mug of beer or mead, glass of wine, shot of alcohol. Moreover it only states &quot;...at least a bit of flair&quot; which means the player does <b>not</b> have to turn the act of drinking the alcohol into an elaborate, by-the-rules, stunt -- they just have to drink in a cool and/or memorable way (hell, the book suggests merely shotgunning a beer and slamming, but not smashing, the mug as sufficient). And, alcohol as a poison is very, <i>very</i> lenient: even without Epic Fortitude, it takes a <i>buttload</i> of alcohol to get drunk, let alone take significant penalties (my scion with his newbie 3 stamina, 3 fortitude has nothing to worry about until his eighth shot).<br /> <br /> It's a once-per-scene knack anyhow, so PC's with the knack can't go on infinite-legend-harvesting pub crawls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Overt Order, Hard Sell (Overt Order's big brother) and Not in the Face... </div> </div> </div>As I said, already got Not the Face. Planning to use it in tandem with Between the Ticks and whatever I have to do to not die. Overt Order and Hard Sell are next on the list, though I <i>might</i> go for Takes One to Know One or Knowing Glance (being able to nuke Willpower pools seems like a good idea for a social character) before Hard Sell.<br /> <br /> I <i>was</i> planning on going pure firearms with the ranged combat knacks and Epic Perception level Stupid with flaming bullets, but considering the extreme difficulty I had talking her into letting me apply Perception to firearm damage (as a knack, nevertheless) I'm not going to bother. She's played Scion before, and probably already knows ranged combat knacks plus clairvoyance equals trouble. Especially when in the course of shooting anything you want at any time and from anywhere, you set everything between yourself and the target on fire, <i>then</i> does the fire purview fun begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 02-27-2014, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T16:07:09-08:00","id":81289,"title":"","content":"I've had some experience playing non combat characters in Scion. A couple suggestions:<br /> <br /> Oh Shit buttons are good. Skin Shedding I recommend to any character. Soliphistic Well Being is useful too depending on perception. If you are a wits guy, invest in talent mirror. You want 1 Epic Stamina minimum anyway, just because you don't want to be the one member of the party who needs to sleep every day when everyone else can go for weeks without, because then you are holding things up.<br /> <br /> One important thing in combat is not to make yourself a target. Some enemies will attack the weak looking ones, especially in an ambush, but more often it makes less sense to go after the weaselly guy not doing much then he huge beserker who is killing two enemies a round. This is obviously something to be sure you are on the same page with your GM about.<br /> <br /> Serpant's Gaze and even moreso Compelling Presence are useful, but tend to draw a lot of hate on you. If you paralyze half the enemy forces with Epic Appearance, expect a lot of attacks coming at you. It is hard to justify enemies not trying to crush someone who frees up half their forces if he goes down.<br /> <br /> If you know magic, one way to keep active and keep your head low is a one-two punch of Trading Fates and Evil Eye. Buff a stronger ally, curse an enemy with your tiny-ass die pool (the max penalty is Presence, so die pool does not matter for that) then your ally should have used their dice and you can buff anouther. Your friends will like the guy who gives someone ~8-10 dice every 10 ticks. In Bohemian Front, Saltmarsh Andy's dice have several times made the difference between the heavy hitters being able to hit and them haivng to use precious legend channels. If you are a Wits/Man guy, as tricksters often are, pick up Paralyzing Confusion. Don't use it unless an enemy comes after you. Stop them, keep buffing and cursing. Illwind Curse is also low level and works well on enemies who use social abilities, but tends to draw more hate then Evil Eye. Andy will also be using Body and Soul and Bards Tongue to buff in time, but that is a Tuatha thing.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T18:10:51-08:00","id":81345,"title":"","content":"I did <b>not</b> even see Talent Mirror when I made the character...okay, definitely getting that one. If I'm reading that right, you can copy the DV of <b>any</b> character your own character has seen dodging something? Because, my character started with Perfect Memory and saw a god dodge something not long after...<br /> <br /> Illwind Curse I was already strongly considering (my character's boons are going to be mostly magic and chaos anyhow), but mainly for comedy factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T20:34:27-08:00","id":81392,"title":"","content":"Social character can be powerful in fight. There are knacks and boons to give 0 DV to an apponent or more : Serpent's Gaze, Compelling Presence, Overt Order, Hard Sell, Heavenly Flare.<br /> To survive there are also Charmer, Engender Love, Not in the Face, Game Face, Dreadful Mien.<br /> <br /> Social character must have Epic Stamina or Epic Dexterity, and also a Stamina, Perception or Wits knack to avoid surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2400-nightbird","name":"Nightbird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T22:51:45-08:00","id":81434,"title":"","content":"Yes. The trick with Talent Mirror is you have to pay to both copy the DV and use the DV, so it quickly becomes an inefficient main defense. It can, however, save your skin if you attract attention till an ally helps you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T04:05:21-08:00","id":81506,"title":"","content":"Depending on how high your Legend goes some of the Justice Purview stuff is silly broken. One lets you bind targets together so if one takes damage so does the other. That can be used to protect yourself from powerful opposition or...to tie something really puny to the big bad and then just wail on the puny thing while the big bad takes damage too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:15:52-08:00","id":83717,"title":"","content":"Sorry to revisit a half-dead thread, but this <i>is</i> my thread and it's still relevant...<br /> <br /> Now, what about contradictory knacks, or knacks that override one another? Like, for example if I have Cat's Grace, then by RAW I can never use Skin-Shedding (the latter talent requires the PC be knocked back, but the former prefers knockdown/back), or if I have Eternal Vigilance or Environmental Awareness, then I can never use Solipsistic Well-Being (since the former two knacks cause auto-detection, and the latter requires the attack be undetected).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T02:21:46-08:00","id":83879,"title":"","content":"I'd say one could elect to use Cat's Grace to prevent KD/KB or allow it because you want to use Skin Shedding. EV/EA is more complicated because you can't really dramatically turn it off for an attack. I'd allow one to turn them off for a scene or whatever and take an action to turn it back on after using SWB, but not switch it reactively like Cat's Grace.<br /> <br /> In general, some pair up better than others, and those which prevent unexpected attacks like EV/EA work poorly with those that react like Rabbit Reflexes, Cobra Reflexes, or SWB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:38:02-08:00","id":84049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat?p=83879#post83879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say one could elect to use Cat's Grace to prevent KD/KB or allow it because you want to use Skin Shedding. EV/EA is more complicated because you can't really dramatically turn it off for an attack. I'd allow one to turn them off for a scene or whatever and take an action to turn it back on after using SWB, but not switch it reactively like Cat's Grace.<br /> <br /> In general, some pair up better than others, and those which prevent unexpected attacks like EV/EA work poorly with those that react like Rabbit Reflexes, Cobra Reflexes, or SWB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah -- I agree completely with interpretation on Cat's Grace and Skin-Shedding, it seems that would be best-interpreted that when skin-shedding cat's grace allows one to land on their feet rather than on their ass/back/whatever (which skin-shedding doesn't rule out), or the player just voluntarily jumps out of their skin to avoid the attack rather than be reactively knocked out of it. It's just the RAW with which I'm concerned, seeing as the book doesn't stipulate knockback can't occur without knockdown (this could be much better-written, seeing that knockback is written as an <i>optional</i> rule which puts skin-shedding's use entirely at the ST's mercy).<br /> <br /> EV with Rabbit Reflexes or Cobra Reflexes seems easier to reconcile through interpretation (at least to me) -- it's just the fluff description rather than mechanics that stand in the way. The way EV is written, it doesn't seem strictly speaking, the scion is <i>conscious</i> of the attack -- they're reacting instinctively (cobra reflexes' description alludes to this). Mechanically, all EV does is allow the scion to automatically join battle when they're ambushed, which gives them a one-tick advantage on the reaction count and allows them to apply standard DV to the first attack. Only rabbit reflexes stipulates anything about joining battle (and then, just the standard disclaimer on joining battle <i>after</i> the surprise attack).<br /> <br /> If I were the ST in that situation, I'd rule the character with EV/RR would auto-join as per EV, but get the double DV on the first tick. With EV/CR, I'd rule the character auto-joins but treat the simultaneous strike as a normal attack action (meaning their next action is up in speed number of ticks). SWB, now that I've given it another read-through specifically in this context, is a lot more clear-cut at least to me since it's based wholly on the character perceiving the attack rather than the element of surprise.<br /> <br /> Either way, it just seems <i>incredibly</i> silly for someone who can look at a place and tell it would make for a good ambush spot (epic mental attributes) regardless whether anyone's actually there, think to themselves &quot;well, this looks like a good ambush spot. I'd better make sure I can't tell if there's going to be one so that if there is, I can ignore the first attack&quot;.<br /> <br /> EA straight-up reads that the PC perceives the attack the instant it occurs (befitting its status as a perception knack) which very much seems like it would negate the relevant wits knacks and SWB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T00:11:37-08:00","id":84442,"title":"","content":"Cat's Grace prevents Knockdown, which requires an entire miscellaneous action to get back up. Skin-Shedding can only be triggered during Knockback. While both of them can trigger as a consequence of a single attack which both knocks you back and knock you down, the two do not contradict each other at all. You can be sent flying back but still land on your feet (and not have to spend a miscellaneous action getting back up) thanks to Cat's Grace.<br /> <br /> Demigod Page 66 clarifies that there are indeed some knacks with are mutually exclusive. It specifically says a character cannot use Rabbit Reflexes or Cobra Reflexes if they have Eternal Vigilance or Environmental Awareness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:46:02-08:00","id":84545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat?p=84442#post84442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cat's Grace prevents Knockdown, which requires an entire miscellaneous action to get back up. Skin-Shedding can only be triggered during Knockback. While both of them can trigger as a consequence of a single attack which both knocks you back and knock you down, the two do not contradict each other at all. You can be sent flying back but still land on your feet (and not have to spend a miscellaneous action getting back up) thanks to Cat's Grace.<br /> <br /> Demigod Page 66 clarifies that there are indeed some knacks with are mutually exclusive. It specifically says a character cannot use Rabbit Reflexes or Cobra Reflexes if they have Eternal Vigilance or Environmental Awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess that settles that in regards to the surprise knacks (though I don't like it). I was under the assumption just CR/RR were incompatible.<br /> <br /> Though, Hero pg. 198 does make it fairly clear knockback is a <i>supplemental</i> and optional consequence of knockdown -- a person cannot be knocked <i>back</i> unless they are also knocked <i>down</i>. Now, I agree with the interpretation the two aren't mutually exclusive and that Cat's Grace shouldn't prevent Skin-Shedding, but RAW is rather vague there and represents a potential snag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T08:59:12-08:00","id":84627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat?p=84545#post84545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, Hero pg. 198 does make it fairly clear knockback is a <i>supplemental</i> and optional consequence of knockdown -- a person cannot be knocked <i>back</i> unless they are also knocked <i>down</i>. Now, I agree with the interpretation the two aren't mutually exclusive and that Cat's Grace shouldn't prevent Skin-Shedding, but RAW is rather vague there and represents a potential snag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the specific wording indicates that you cannot knock back unless you would also be knocked down, which would literally mean that someone with Cat's Grace cannot be knocked back. Neither can anyone who overcomes a difficulty 2 (Dexterity + Athletics) or (Stamina + Fortitude) roll. It becomes storyteller decisions as to whether knock back is independent of knockdown (since there are specific effects listed elsewhere that knock back without knocking down), and whether or not you can voluntarily fail the roll difficulty 2 roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T14:27:13-08:00","id":84848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80701-non-combat-scions-in-combat?p=84627#post84627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the specific wording indicates that you cannot knock back unless you would also be knocked down, which would literally mean that someone with Cat's Grace cannot be knocked back. Neither can anyone who overcomes a difficulty 2 (Dexterity + Athletics) or (Stamina + Fortitude) roll. It becomes storyteller decisions as to whether knock back is independent of knockdown (since there are specific effects listed elsewhere that knock back without knocking down), and whether or not you can voluntarily fail the roll difficulty 2 roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the part in particular that makes me cock my head and say &quot;...huh?&quot;, especially since a character could have enough (Sta+Fort), but not enough health levels via epic stamina, to not suffer knockdown from an attack that would instagib them which would mean skin-shedding could not actually save them. I'm not saying it's a <i>likely</i> possibility, just a <i>possible</i> one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}